      "receiptId": "sambocade.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Forme of Cury\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by the Chief Master-Cook of King Richard II, c1390 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#cury-1390\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ECury 1390\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003ESAMBOCADE\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake and make a Crust in a trape. \u0026 take a cruddes and wryng out \u00FEe wheyze. and drawe hem \u00FEurgh a straynour and put in \u00FEe straynour crustes. do \u00FEerto sugur the \u00FEridde part \u0026 somdel [2] whyte of Ayrenn. \u0026 shake \u00FEerin blomes of elren [3]. \u0026 bake it up with curose [4] \u0026 messe it forth.\u003Cbr\u003E\n[1] Sambucade. As made of the Sambucus, or Elder. [2] Somdel. Some. [3] Blom of Elren. Elder flowers. [4] curose\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
